# Table Reservation & Management System

---

## 🧪 End-to-End Testing
The automated E2E test suite for this application is maintained in a dedicated repository:  
👉 **[View Playwright E2E Test Suite](https://github.com/htrauzer/playwright_automation_suite.git)**

---

## 📌 Project Overview

This project simulates an interactive restaurant layout where clients can select and reserve tables based on their specific preferences:
- **Date & Time:** Reserve tables for specific time slots.
- **Party Size:** Filter tables suitable for the number of guests.
- **Zone Preference:** Choose seating options based on restaurant zones (e.g., Main Hall, Terrace, VIP).
- **Reservation Form:** Interactive booking flow with immediate confirmation handling.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Python (FastAPI / ASGI server framework)
- **Database:** SQLite
- **Frontend:** JavaScript (Vanilla ES6+), HTML5, CSS3
- **Server Runner:** Uvicorn

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

### 1. Prerequisites
Before running the project, make sure you have installed:
- **Python 3.8+**
- **FastAPI:** `pip install fastapi`
- **Uvicorn:** `pip install "uvicorn[standard]"`

### 2. Installation
Clone the repository and install required dependencies:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/table_reservation_and_mangement.git
cd table_reservation_and_mangement

python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 3. Run the Application
Launch the development server using Uvicorn:
```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Once running, open your browser and navigate to:
```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 🗺️ **Visual Floor Plan Layout:** Interactive UI mapping out restaurant tables and zones.
- 📅 **Dynamic Scheduling:** Check table availability dynamically across selected dates and times.
- 👥 **Capacity Filtering:** Match party sizes with appropriate table seating capacities.
- 📝 **Reservation Form:** Streamlined client interface for entering booking details.
- 💾 **SQLite Integration:** Persistence layer storing table definitions, availability statuses, and active reservations.

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```text

table_reservation_and_mangement/
│
├── main.py                     # The "Start Button" (Only initializes the app)
├── database/                   # Everything SQL & DB related
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── connection.py           # Engine & SessionLocal setup
│   └── models.py               # SQLAlchemy Database Models
│
├── api/                        # Router modules split by domain
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── schemas.py              # Pydantic schemas (Request/Response validation)
│   ├── reservations.py         # Guest & Admin Reservation endpoints
│   └── tables.py               # Physical Layout Management endpoints 
│
├── services/                   # The "Brain" of your application
|    ├── __init__.py
|    └── reservation_service.py # Core algorithms, table-matching logic, time-slot sorting
|
├── errors/                     # Custom exceptions and global handlers
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── handlers.py
│
├── tests/                      # Regressive automated testing suite
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── test_reservations.py
│
├── templates/                  # Frontend HTML/CSS layouts (If serving pages)
│   └── index.html
│
├──static
│   ├── css/styles.css
│   └── js/app.js
│
└─ README.md                    # Project documentation